    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:569e72e117968fcc",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "2c9405b4ae6a702f043736e415b0476ebcc27b22f3319d86f2d3d08fa0713c4f",
      "text": "An early start from San José (around 6:00) by air-conditioned bus with a bilingual naturalist guide, through Braulio Carrillo National Park and its abundant vegetation. Breakfast at the Selva Tropical restaurant, with its butterfly garden and tropical flowers, then on past banana plantations to the Caño Blanco dock, where a covered boat takes you along the Tortuguero canals to the lodge (arrival around 12:30–13:00). In the afternoon, visit the visitor centre of the Sea Turtle Conservancy (formerly the Caribbean Conservation Corporation) and the colourful village of Tortuguero; return to the lodge around 17:30. Free time to enjoy the pool and bar; dinner from 19:30 to 21:00. Overnight at Pachira Lodge. (B, L, D)",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_aligned",
